// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: the mv layer mints a SECOND map slot for the `{[K2]: V} | null`
// spelling of a value whose NON-NULL twin already has one, and `mvTwin` does not merge
// them — so one map layout gets two heap types and a store crosses between them.
//
// SEVEN LINES, no function, no union, no generic, no import, no lambda, no `??`, and one
// annotation. `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics at all and is the ONLY command that
// misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1,
// `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The message is the stable
//  identifier — and the NULLABILITY in it is NOT the mechanism. Disassembled, the two
//  `$type`s are two STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL map structs at different indices, one minted
//  for `{[string]: {[string]: i32}}` and one for `{[string]: {[string]: i32} | null}`.
//  This is the third specimen in a row whose sentence mentions nullability and whose
//  mechanism is two heap types; read the DISASSEMBLY, never the sentence.)
//
// THE AXIS IS THE SECOND SPELLING, not the nullability and not the nesting. Drop the
// `| null` from the annotation and it runs; make the inner map MONO (`{[string]: i32}`,
// whose struct is the shared one) and it runs; annotate `l2` with the same nullable-valued
// spelling the outer carries and it runs. It needs a map layout named twice, once bare
// and once `| null`, with the bare one inferred and the nullable one annotated.
//
// PRE-EXISTING on `7b600b57`, same sentence — not a regression from the change this file
// ships with. Filed as `silent-class-inventory.md` D124; on the 1,114-cell D112 grid it is
// 33 of the 61 surviving silent cells.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member
// of the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT —
// including what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty, and the
// sixth source it carries: re-grade an EARLIER change's grid against today's master.
const z = Map()
z["z"] = 1
const l2 = Map()
l2["a"] = z
const c: {[string]: {[string]: {[string]: i32} | null}} = Map()
c["k"] = l2
print(7)
